description KCD, 37 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) 2026-10-22, build fda4ec7; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, up to the pause menu at its end, 56.5 s to 2305.0 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 14
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.7
field_pull_wraps 32
# WHAT IT COVERS: the first stream of 2026-10-22, from a relay launch of its own, 37.5 minutes
# cut to the gameplay its video shows, captured through NvFBC on the defaults and the policy the
# tree ships. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 256 times (410 an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or
# more 34 times (54 an hour), in 59 bursts, 22 of them with a stall, and with no periodic stretch.
# Its rarest part is a scripted horseback chase at 2004.8 to 2008.9 s: 58 hitches in 4 s with no
# stall, where the game's frame times swung widely and the relay's present blocked for about
# 33 ms 33 times; it is kept as a pathological case. The lock released 5 times in the field (at
# 369.35, 1845.19, 1995.01, 2005.93 and 2211.73 s) and 4 times on the replay, at the same
# moments except 1845.2 s. The replay's worst blend run, 30 presents from 369.15 s, sits at a
# pull wrap. Of the 31 moves on the replay, 1 lands more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 56.501 s, from the 2039
# marked frames in its first 33 s, all on time and within 0.41 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 2255.3 s with no holes and opens on marked gameplay (a map is open for a few seconds
# before the first minute ends); it ends on the pause menu from about 2249 s of video, so the
# cut ends at 2305.0 s of log time and starts at 56.5 s, and the marked frames lie inside it.
# Inside the cut, 20 seconds in 17 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime: 16 single hitch seconds
# and the 4 s chase above, left in on purpose.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line (the plain arm) reads synth 0.8% against 0.7%, worst run 30 against 14, runs >= 50
# 0 against 0 and pull wraps 32 against 32. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran and
# what the counts here use, blends are 977 against 943, repeats 257 against 258, skips 118
# against 119, pull wraps 32 against 32 and the worst run 30 against 14. The worst run is the one
# number outside the corpus's fidelity limits: at 369.15 s the field wrapped its pull upward at
# 369.33 s and blended in runs of 4 and 6, while the replay's pull drifted down by 25 us a present
# about 7 ms from the nearest frame and blended 30 presents in a row until a hard jump. The
# replay misreads how the pull moves right after a burst of hitches; the bound on the worst run
# holds the replay's own 30, so it still catches a change that lengthens it. The replay makes 31
# moves, 8 of them late, and the field's log has 34 in the window.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 30
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.2
min_reseeds 55
max_pull_wraps 32
extra_lag_ms 75
arrivals 264000
